<title>USA: CME feeder cattle tumble on soaring CBOT corn.</title>
<headline>CME feeder cattle tumble on soaring CBOT corn.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME feeder cattle futures fell sharply as CBOT corn futures soared their 12-cent-a-bushel limit on many contracts in early trade.</p>
<p>September feeders sunk to a low of 80.350 cents a lb, down 0.925 cent as corn prices surged on concern that hot, dry weather in the U.S. Midwest could hamper pollination.</p>
<p>((Nigel Hunt 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
